<title>BRAZIL: Paranagua operating at full capacity-official.</title>
<headline>Paranagua operating at full capacity-official.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The key Brazilian port of Paranagua was functioning normally and current loadings were not affected by a dispute with dockworkers over pay, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are operating at full capacity,&quot; she said. &quot;Loadings of soybeans and soymeal are taking place 24 hours a day.&quot;  </p>
<p>She added that negotiations were taking place at a national level on dockworkers' demands for a 21 percent wage increase which they say they were promised last year, but she could not say where the talks currently stood.</p>
<p>A Paranagua union official earlier told Reuters that the port was working at less than 50 percent of its normal capacity since Saturday night and that loadings were affected.</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417))</p>
